/-!
# Stacks 07SQ fails without the chapter's convention on the site

The chapter on limits of algebraic spaces works under the convention of its Section 70.2 (tag
07SD) that every ring it considers has its spectrum in the big fppf site. Read for an inverse
system of algebraic spaces this is `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SiteContainsBaseChangeLimits`, and
Stacks 07SQ, namely
`DescentSituation.exists_isAffineSpace_system_obj_of_siteContainsBaseChangeLimits` in the same
namespace, is proved under it. This file shows that the hypothesis cannot be dropped.

Let `B` be a big fppf site containing the terminal scheme and let `F` be a field whose
cardinality is at least the cutoff of `B`. For a finite subset `T ⊆ F` let `A_T` be the subring
of `F` it generates, and let `X_T = 𝔸²_{A_T} ∖ V(x, y)` be the punctured plane over it. The
`X_T` form a directed inverse system, indexed by the finite subsets of `F`, of quasi-compact
quasi-separated schemes with affine transition morphisms, and every `A_T` is countable, so every
`X_T` lies in `B`. No `X_T` is affine, since `A_T` is nonzero. A scheme `Z` of the site carrying
compatible morphisms to all the `X_T` carries compatible ring homomorphisms from all the `A_T`
to a stalk of `Z` at any point; these are injective on `F`, while a stalk of `Z` is smaller than
the cutoff. So `Z` is empty, and the limit of the system, in the site and hence in presheaves on
it, is the empty scheme: an affine algebraic space. The convention fails for this system, as it
must: the colimit of the `A_T` is `F`, whose spectrum is not in the site.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SiteConventionCounterexample.puncturedPlaneFunctor`: the punctured
  plane, as a functor of the base ring.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SiteConventionCounterexample.descentSituation`: the system above, as
  a situation of Stacks 084R over the terminal scheme.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SiteConventionCounterexample.isAffineSpace_limitCone_pt`: its limit
  is an affine algebraic space.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SiteConventionCounterexample.not_isAffineSpace_system_obj`: none of
  its stages is.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SiteConventionCounterexample.not_siteContainsBaseChangeLimits`: it
  violates the convention.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.DescentSituation.not_forall_exists_isAffineSpace_system_obj`: the
  statement of Stacks 07SQ with the convention dropped is false.

## Implementation notes

That the system violates the convention is deduced from Stacks 07SQ itself, which holds under
the convention and whose conclusion fails here. The base is the terminal scheme, over which
every scheme of the site is an object of the site in a unique way; the statement refuted
quantifies over the base, so one base suffices.

The same field gives the counterexample the implementation notes of
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.DescendingProperties.AffineMorphismDescent` describe for
Stacks 084Y, with the spectra of the finitely generated subfields of `F` as the system of bases.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 07SD](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07SD)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07SQ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07SQ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 084R](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/084R)
-/

@[expose] public section

noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite Cardinal

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SiteConventionCounterexample

open Stacks.Refute09ZM

/-! ### Compatible maps out of the finitely generated subrings of a field -/

/-- A family of ring homomorphisms from the subrings of a field `F` generated by its finite
subsets into a nonzero ring, compatible with the inclusions, is injective on `F`: read at the
singletons, it separates any two distinct elements `x` and `y`, because `x - y` is a unit of the
subring generated by `{x, y, (x - y)⁻¹}`. -/
theorem injective_of_compatible_closureMaps {F : Type*} [Field F] {A : Type*} [CommRing A]
    [Nontrivial A] (ψ : (T : Finset F) → Subring.closure (↑T : Set F) →+* A)
    (hψ : ∀ (T T' : Finset F), T ⊆ T' → ∀ (x : F) (hx : x ∈ Subring.closure (↑T : Set F))
        (hx' : x ∈ Subring.closure (↑T' : Set F)), ψ T' ⟨x, hx'⟩ = ψ T ⟨x, hx⟩) :
    Function.Injective (fun x : F => ψ {x} ⟨x, Subring.subset_closure (by simp)⟩) := by
  classical
  intro x y hxy
  simp only at hxy
  by_contra hne
  have hd : x - y ≠ 0 := sub_ne_zero_of_ne hne
  set T : Finset F := {x, y, (x - y)⁻¹} with hT
  have hmem : ∀ z ∈ T, z ∈ Subring.closure (↑T : Set F) := fun z hz => Subring.subset_closure hz
  have hsing : ∀ (z : F) (hz : z ∈ T), ψ T ⟨z, hmem z hz⟩ =
      ψ {z} ⟨z, Subring.subset_closure (by simp)⟩ :=
    fun z hz => hψ {z} T (by simpa using hz) z _ _
  have hx : x ∈ T := by simp [hT]
  have hy : y ∈ T := by simp [hT]
  have hi : (x - y)⁻¹ ∈ T := by simp [hT]
  have key : (⟨x, hmem x hx⟩ - ⟨y, hmem y hy⟩ : Subring.closure (↑T : Set F)) *
      ⟨(x - y)⁻¹, hmem _ hi⟩ = 1 := by
    apply Subtype.ext
    push_cast
    field_simp
  have hcon := congrArg (ψ T) key
  rw [map_one, map_mul, map_sub, hsing x hx, hsing y hy, hxy] at hcon
  simp at hcon

variable (F : Type u) [Field F]

/-- The subring of a field generated by a finite set is countable: it is the image of a
polynomial ring over `ℤ` in finitely many variables. -/
instance countable_closure (T : Finset F) : Countable (Subring.closure (↑T : Set F)) := by
  have hset : ((Subring.closure (↑T : Set F) : Subring F) : Set F)
      = Set.range (MvPolynomial.aeval (R := ℤ) (Subtype.val : (↑T : Set F) → F)) := by
    have h := Algebra.adjoin_eq_range ℤ (↑T : Set F)
    rw [Algebra.adjoin_int] at h
    exact congrArg (fun S : Subalgebra ℤ F => (S : Set F)) h
  change Countable ((Subring.closure (↑T : Set F) : Subring F) : Set F)
  rw [hset]
  exact (Set.countable_range _).to_subtype

/-- The subring of `F` generated by a finite subset, as a commutative ring. -/
abbrev closureObj (T : Finset F) : CommRingCat.{u} := CommRingCat.of (Subring.closure (↑T : Set F))

/-- The inclusion of the subrings of `F` generated by two nested finite subsets. -/
def closureMap {T T' : Finset F} (h : T ≤ T') : closureObj F T ⟶ closureObj F T' :=
  CommRingCat.ofHom (Subring.inclusion (Subring.closure_mono (Finset.coe_subset.mpr h)))

/-- `closureMap` at the reflexive inclusion is the identity. -/
theorem closureMap_id (T : Finset F) : closureMap F (le_refl T) = 𝟙 _ :=
  rfl

/-- `closureMap` sends the composite of two nested inclusions to the composite of the maps. -/
theorem closureMap_comp {T T' T'' : Finset F} (h : T ≤ T') (h' : T' ≤ T'') :
    closureMap F (h.trans h') = closureMap F h ≫ closureMap F h' := by
  refine CommRingCat.hom_ext (RingHom.ext fun x => ?_)
  rw [CommRingCat.hom_comp, RingHom.comp_apply, closureMap, closureMap, closureMap,
    CommRingCat.hom_ofHom, CommRingCat.hom_ofHom, CommRingCat.hom_ofHom]
  exact Subtype.ext (by rw [Subring.coe_inclusion, Subring.coe_inclusion, Subring.coe_inclusion])

/-- The directed system of the subrings of `F` generated by its finite subsets. -/
def closureRing : Finset F ⥤ CommRingCat.{u} where
  obj T := closureObj F T
  map h := closureMap F (leOfHom h)
  map_id _ := closureMap_id F _
  map_comp f g := closureMap_comp F (leOfHom f) (leOfHom g)

/-! ### The punctured plane as a functor of the base ring -/

/-- The punctured plane `𝔸²_A ∖ V(x, y)` over a commutative ring `A`, as a contravariant functor
of `A`. -/
def puncturedPlaneFunctor : CommRingCat.{u}ᵒᵖ ⥤ Scheme.{u} where
  obj R := punctured R.unop
  map {R R'} φ := (specPlaneMap φ.unop.hom).resLE _ _
    (le_of_eq (preimage_puncturedOpen φ.unop.hom).symm)
  map_id R := by
    rw [← cancel_mono (puncturedOpen R.unop).ι, Scheme.Hom.resLE_comp_ι, Category.id_comp,
      unop_id, CommRingCat.hom_id, specPlaneMap_id, Category.comp_id]
  map_comp {R₁ R₂ R₃} f g := by
    rw [← cancel_mono (puncturedOpen R₃.unop).ι, Scheme.Hom.resLE_comp_ι, Category.assoc,
      Scheme.Hom.resLE_comp_ι, Scheme.Hom.resLE_comp_ι_assoc, unop_comp, CommRingCat.hom_comp,
      specPlaneMap_comp]

/-- The morphisms of punctured planes induced by ring homomorphisms are affine. -/
instance isAffineHom_puncturedPlaneFunctor_map {R R' : CommRingCat.{u}ᵒᵖ} (φ : R ⟶ R') :
    _root_.AlgebraicGeometry.IsAffineHom (puncturedPlaneFunctor.map φ) :=
  isAffineHom_resLE_of_eq _ (preimage_puncturedOpen φ.unop.hom).symm

/-- The structure morphism of the punctured plane over the spectrum of its base ring, natural in
the ring. -/
def puncturedPlaneToSpec : puncturedPlaneFunctor.{u} ⟶ Scheme.Spec where
  app R := (puncturedOpen R.unop).ι ≫ specPlaneBase R.unop
  naturality {R R'} φ := by
    dsimp only [puncturedPlaneFunctor]
    rw [Scheme.Hom.resLE_comp_ι_assoc, specPlaneMap_comp_specPlaneBase, Category.assoc]
    rfl

/-- The system of punctured planes over the subrings of `F` generated by its finite subsets. -/
def puncturedPlaneSystem : (Finset F)ᵒᵖ ⥤ Scheme.{u} :=
  (closureRing F).op ⋙ puncturedPlaneFunctor

/-- The structure morphism of a stage of `puncturedPlaneSystem` over the spectrum of its base
ring. -/
def stageToSpec (T : Finset F) :
    (puncturedPlaneSystem F).obj (op T) ⟶ Spec (closureObj F T) :=
  puncturedPlaneToSpec.app (op (closureObj F T))

/-- The transition morphisms of `puncturedPlaneSystem` commute with `stageToSpec` and the
morphisms of spectra induced by `closureMap`. -/
theorem map_comp_stageToSpec {T T' : Finset F} (h : T ≤ T') :
    (puncturedPlaneSystem F).map (homOfLE h).op ≫ stageToSpec F T =
      stageToSpec F T' ≫ Spec.map (closureMap F h) :=
  puncturedPlaneToSpec.naturality ((closureRing F).map (homOfLE h)).op

/-- **A scheme mapping compatibly to every stage is empty, unless it is as large as `F`.** The
structure morphisms to the spectra of the subrings of `F` give, on global functions followed by
the germ at a point, a compatible family of ring homomorphisms into a stalk, which is injective
on `F` by `injective_of_compatible_closureMaps`; and a stalk is no larger than the scheme. -/
theorem isEmpty_of_compatible {X : Scheme.{u}} (hX : X.size < #F)
    (g : ∀ T : Finset F, X ⟶ (puncturedPlaneSystem F).obj (op T))
    (hg : ∀ (T T' : Finset F) (h : T ≤ T'),
      g T' ≫ (puncturedPlaneSystem F).map (homOfLE h).op = g T) : IsEmpty X := by
  refine ⟨fun z => ?_⟩
  let leg : ∀ T, X ⟶ Spec (closureObj F T) := fun T => g T ≫ stageToSpec F T
  have hleg : ∀ (T T' : Finset F) (h : T ≤ T'),
      leg T' ≫ Spec.map (closureMap F h) = leg T := by
    intro T T' h
    simp only [leg, Category.assoc]
    rw [← map_comp_stageToSpec, ← Category.assoc, hg T T' h]
  let ψ : (T : Finset F) → Subring.closure (↑T : Set F) →+* X.presheaf.stalk z := fun T =>
    ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (closureObj F T)).inv ≫ (leg T).appTop ≫ X.presheaf.germ ⊤ z trivial).hom
  have hψ : ∀ (T T' : Finset F), T ⊆ T' → ∀ (x : F) (hx : x ∈ Subring.closure (↑T : Set F))
      (hx' : x ∈ Subring.closure (↑T' : Set F)), ψ T' ⟨x, hx'⟩ = ψ T ⟨x, hx⟩ := by
    intro T T' h x hx hx'
    have key : (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (closureObj F T)).inv ≫ (leg T).appTop =
        closureMap F h ≫ (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (closureObj F T')).inv ≫ (leg T').appTop := by
      rw [← Category.assoc, Scheme.ΓSpecIso_inv_naturality, Category.assoc,
        ← Scheme.Hom.comp_appTop, hleg T T' h]
    show ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (closureObj F T')).inv ≫ (leg T').appTop ≫ _).hom ⟨x, hx'⟩ =
      ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (closureObj F T)).inv ≫ (leg T).appTop ≫ _).hom ⟨x, hx⟩
    rw [← Category.assoc, ← Category.assoc (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (closureObj F T)).inv, key]
    rfl
  exact not_le.mpr hX ((Cardinal.mk_le_of_injective
    (injective_of_compatible_closureMaps ψ hψ)).trans (X.mk_stalk_le_size z))

/-! ### The system in the big fppf site -/

/-- **Every stage lies in every big fppf site.** It is an open subscheme of the affine plane
over a countable ring, and the cutoff of a site is uncountable and closed under the passage to
subobjects. -/
theorem contains_puncturedPlaneSystem_obj (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (T : Finset F) :
    B.Contains ((puncturedPlaneSystem F).obj (op T)) := by
  have hplane : B.Contains (affinePlane (Subring.closure (↑T : Set F))) := by
    show (Spec _).size < B.cutoff
    rw [Scheme.size_Spec]
    exact max_lt B.aleph0_lt_cutoff (Cardinal.mk_le_aleph0.trans_lt B.aleph0_lt_cutoff)
  exact Scheme.size_lt_of_mono_of_isStrongPrelimit (X := punctured (Subring.closure (↑T : Set F)))
    B.cutoff_isStrongPrelimit (puncturedOpen (Subring.closure (↑T : Set F))).ι hplane

variable (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (hZ : B.Contains (⊤_ Scheme.{u}))

/-- An object of the big fppf site whose underlying scheme is empty is initial. -/
def isInitialOfIsEmptyToScheme {S : Scheme.{u}} {hS : B.Contains S} (Z : BigFppfOver B S hS)
    [h : IsEmpty ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj Z)] : IsInitial Z :=
  haveI : IsEmpty (B.inclusion.obj Z.left) := h
  haveI : IsEmpty (Over.left Z).obj := h
  IsInitial.ofUniqueHom
    (fun _ => Over.homMk (ObjectProperty.homMk (isInitialOfIsEmpty.to _))
      (B.inclusion.map_injective (isInitialOfIsEmpty.hom_ext _ _)))
    (fun _ _ => Over.OverMorphism.ext (B.inclusion.map_injective (isInitialOfIsEmpty.hom_ext _ _)))

/-- The system of punctured planes over the finitely generated subrings of `F`, as a system of
objects of the big fppf site over the terminal scheme. -/
def siteSystem : (Finset F)ᵒᵖ ⥤ BigFppfOver B (⊤_ Scheme.{u}) hZ where
  obj T := siteObject B (⊤_ Scheme.{u}) hZ (contains_puncturedPlaneSystem_obj F B T.unop)
    (terminal.from _)
  map f := Over.homMk (ObjectProperty.homMk ((puncturedPlaneSystem F).map f))
    (B.inclusion.map_injective (terminal.hom_ext _ _))
  map_id T := Over.OverMorphism.ext (B.inclusion.map_injective ((puncturedPlaneSystem F).map_id T))
  map_comp f g :=
    Over.OverMorphism.ext (B.inclusion.map_injective ((puncturedPlaneSystem F).map_comp f g))

/-- The empty scheme, as an object of the big fppf site over the terminal scheme. -/
abbrev emptyObject : BigFppfOver B (⊤_ Scheme.{u}) hZ :=
  siteObject B (⊤_ Scheme.{u}) hZ B.contains_empty (terminal.from _)

/-- The underlying scheme of `emptyObject` is empty. -/
instance isEmpty_toScheme_emptyObject :
    IsEmpty ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B (⊤_ Scheme.{u}) hZ).obj (emptyObject B hZ)) :=
  inferInstanceAs (IsEmpty (∅ : Scheme.{u}))

/-- The cone over `siteSystem` with the empty scheme as vertex. -/
def siteLimitCone : Cone (siteSystem F B hZ) where
  pt := emptyObject B hZ
  π :=
    { app := fun _ => (isInitialOfIsEmptyToScheme B (emptyObject B hZ)).to _
      naturality := fun _ _ _ => (isInitialOfIsEmptyToScheme B (emptyObject B hZ)).hom_ext _ _ }

/-- **Every cone over `siteSystem` in the site has an empty vertex**, as soon as `F` is at least
as large as the cutoff of the site: the vertex is an object of the site, hence smaller than `F`,
and `isEmpty_of_compatible` applies. -/
theorem isEmpty_toScheme_cone_pt (hF : B.cutoff ≤ #F) (s : Cone (siteSystem F B hZ)) :
    IsEmpty ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B (⊤_ Scheme.{u}) hZ).obj s.pt) :=
  isEmpty_of_compatible F (lt_of_lt_of_le s.pt.left.property hF)
    (fun T => (BigFppfOver.toScheme B (⊤_ Scheme.{u}) hZ).map (s.π.app (op T)))
    (fun T T' h => by
      show _ ≫ (BigFppfOver.toScheme B (⊤_ Scheme.{u}) hZ).map
        ((siteSystem F B hZ).map (homOfLE h).op) = _
      rw [← Functor.map_comp, Cone.w])

/-- **The limit of `siteSystem` in the site is the empty scheme.** -/
def isLimitSiteLimitCone (hF : B.cutoff ≤ #F) : IsLimit (siteLimitCone F B hZ) where
  lift s :=
    haveI := isEmpty_toScheme_cone_pt F B hZ hF s
    (isInitialOfIsEmptyToScheme B s.pt).to _
  fac s _ :=
    haveI := isEmpty_toScheme_cone_pt F B hZ hF s
    (isInitialOfIsEmptyToScheme B s.pt).hom_ext _ _
  uniq s _ _ :=
    haveI := isEmpty_toScheme_cone_pt F B hZ hF s
    (isInitialOfIsEmptyToScheme B s.pt).hom_ext _ _

/-- **The counterexample**, as a situation of Stacks 084R over the terminal scheme: the
directed system, indexed by the finite subsets of `F`, of the algebraic spaces represented by
the punctured planes over the subrings of `F` they generate, with the limit represented by the
empty scheme. -/
def descentSituation (hF : B.cutoff ≤ #F) :
    DescentSituation B (⊤_ Scheme.{u}) hZ hZ (Finset F) where
  system := siteSystem F B hZ ⋙ yoneda
  algebraicSpace _ := isAlgebraicSpace_yoneda B _ hZ _
  transition_affine _ := isAffineHom_of_presheaf
    ((presheaf_yoneda_map_iff B _ hZ (P := @_root_.AlgebraicGeometry.IsAffineHom.{u})
      inferInstance _).mpr (isAffineHom_puncturedPlaneFunctor_map _))
  quasiCompact _ := isQuasiCompactSpace_yoneda B _ hZ _
    (inferInstanceAs (CompactSpace (punctured _)))
  quasiSeparated _ := isAbsolutelyQuasiSeparated_of_isQuasiSeparatedScheme B _ hZ _ hZ
    ⟨_, inferInstanceAs (QuasiSeparatedSpace (punctured _)), ⟨Functor.RepresentableBy.yoneda _⟩⟩
  limitCone := yoneda.mapCone (siteLimitCone F B hZ)
  isLimit := isLimitOfPreserves yoneda (isLimitSiteLimitCone F B hZ hF)
  limitAlgebraicSpace := isAlgebraicSpace_yoneda B _ hZ _
  base := ∅

/-- **The limit of the counterexample is an affine algebraic space**: it is represented by the
empty scheme. -/
theorem isAffineSpace_limitCone_pt (hF : B.cutoff ≤ #F) :
    IsAffineSpace B (⊤_ Scheme.{u}) hZ (descentSituation F B hZ hF).limitCone.pt :=
  isAffineSpace_yoneda B _ hZ _ (@isAffine_of_isEmpty _ (isEmpty_toScheme_emptyObject B hZ))

/-- **No stage of the counterexample is an affine algebraic space**: a representable presheaf
isomorphic to one represented by an affine scheme is represented by an isomorphic scheme, and a
punctured plane over a nonzero ring is not affine. -/
theorem not_isAffineSpace_system_obj (hF : B.cutoff ≤ #F) (T : Finset F) :
    ¬ IsAffineSpace B (⊤_ Scheme.{u}) hZ ((descentSituation F B hZ hF).system.obj (op T)) := by
  rintro ⟨W, hW, ⟨e⟩⟩
  have : IsAffine ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B _ hZ).obj ((siteSystem F B hZ).obj (op T))) :=
    IsAffine.of_isIso
      ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B _ hZ).mapIso (Yoneda.fullyFaithful.preimageIso e)).hom
  exact not_isAffine_punctured (Subring.closure (↑T : Set F)) this

/-- **The counterexample violates the chapter's convention.** Were
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SiteContainsBaseChangeLimits` to hold for it, Stacks 07SQ,
`DescentSituation.exists_isAffineSpace_system_obj_of_siteContainsBaseChangeLimits`, would give an
affine stage, since the limit is affine. -/
theorem not_siteContainsBaseChangeLimits (hF : B.cutoff ≤ #F) :
    ¬ SiteContainsBaseChangeLimits B (⊤_ Scheme.{u}) hZ (descentSituation F B hZ hF).system := by
  intro hconv
  obtain ⟨i, -, hi⟩ :=
    (descentSituation F B hZ hF).exists_isAffineSpace_system_obj_of_siteContainsBaseChangeLimits
      hconv (isAffineSpace_limitCone_pt F B hZ hF)
  exact not_isAffineSpace_system_obj F B hZ hF i hi

/-! ### A field as large as the cutoff -/

/-- A type of the cardinality of the cutoff of a big fppf site. -/
def cutoffField (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) : Type u := B.cutoff.out

/-- The cardinality of `cutoffField B` is the cutoff of `B`. -/
theorem mk_cutoffField : #(cutoffField B) = B.cutoff := Cardinal.mk_out _

/-- It carries a field structure, the cutoff being infinite. -/
instance field_cutoffField : Field (cutoffField B) :=
  Classical.choice (@Infinite.nonempty_field _ (Cardinal.infinite_iff.mpr
    ((mk_cutoffField B).symm ▸ B.aleph0_lt_cutoff.le)))

end SiteConventionCounterexample

open SiteConventionCounterexample in
/-- **Stacks 07SQ is false without the chapter's convention on the site.** The statement of
`DescentSituation.exists_isAffineSpace_system_obj_of_siteContainsBaseChangeLimits` with its
hypothesis `SiteContainsBaseChangeLimits` dropped fails: over the terminal scheme of a big fppf
site containing it, the directed system of punctured planes over the subrings generated by the
finite subsets of a field as large as the cutoff is a situation of Stacks 084R whose limit is
affine and none of whose stages is. -/
theorem DescentSituation.not_forall_exists_isAffineSpace_system_obj :
    ¬ ∀ (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)
        (hZ : B.Contains (⊤_ Scheme.{u})) (I : Type u) [Preorder I] [IsDirected I (· ≤ ·)]
        (D : DescentSituation B S hS hZ I),
        IsAffineSpace B S hS D.limitCone.pt →
          ∃ i, D.base ≤ i ∧ IsAffineSpace B S hS (D.system.obj (op i)) := by
  intro h
  obtain ⟨B, hZ⟩ := BigFppfSite.exists_contains (⊤_ Scheme.{u})
  have hF : B.cutoff ≤ #(cutoffField B) := (mk_cutoffField B).ge
  obtain ⟨i, -, hi⟩ := h B _ hZ hZ _ (descentSituation (cutoffField B) B hZ hF)
    (isAffineSpace_limitCone_pt _ B hZ hF)
  exact not_isAffineSpace_system_obj _ B hZ hF i hi

end AlgebraicGeometry.Space
